    "memoText": " \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 189\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 2138, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  workers'  compensation law, in relation to\n      including coverage of treatment rendered by a massage therapist\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would amend the Workers' Compensation Law  to  add  licensed\nmassage  therapists  to  the  list  of  authorized providers of workers'\ncompensation services.\n \n  Massage therapy may provide short-term  relief  and  have  therapeutic\nvalue,  but  it  is  very difficult to measure the impact of a course of\nmassage on an injured worker's functional ability. Medical treatment and\ncare under the Workers' Compensation  Law  is  strictly  evidence-based;\ndocumentation of demonstrable functional improvement must be shown.\n \n  Massage  therapy  codes,  when  part  of a treatment plan, are already\navailable for physicians and other limited health care providers provid-\ning treatment to injured workers. However, massage therapy is not recom-\nmended in the majority of  the  Workers'  Compensation  Board's  medical\ntreatment  guidelines.  Absent  the  ability to quantify the benefits to\nindividuals, this expansion has the potential to greatly increase  costs\nto ensure it is properly administered.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this legislation.\n \n  This bill is disapproved.                      (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 189,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2022
   }
